{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Variation_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Variation of Solution 1)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is a perfect square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3573192f9a46164606a2e832697446e87ce54be8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{14!15!}2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{15!16!}2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{16!17!}2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{17!18!}2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{18!19!}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"554\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for all positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6cadcea118b402a6a8d08b9ed33371afc4b43a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{n!(n+1)!}{2}\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f4a73e6e6c4cc24be518527f91d6a867e8f5b24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies\\dfrac{(n!)^2\\cdot(n+1)}{2}\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2130d4422339b6c4b17ef79fc45d476fffa67ed2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies (n!)^2\\cdot\\dfrac{n+1}{2}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>We must find a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9f5a7c3ca6a90790ab24d89fb9b52e4db243cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n!)^2\\cdot\\dfrac{n+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" /> is a perfect square. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25026d3bff73b1ac5b5db10da7f4574b44c2c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n!)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"19\" /> is a perfect square, we must also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36ff83257ab4ee6b8fa29edf847deb73d5778815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> be a perfect square. \n</p><p>In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36ff83257ab4ee6b8fa29edf847deb73d5778815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> to be a perfect square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> must be twice a perfect square. From the answer choices, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db87b72bc789ff77938cb04ba4a5d41cdfcf193b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> works, thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5a50f89eb87941facbb1e7b1ae91777fa10f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> and our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69aa9273fab09663f313366e7a0cbad049d5529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{17!18!}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"97\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Variation_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Variation_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (Variation of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Variation of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We take the first option A. \\( \\frac{14! \\cdot 15!}{2} \\). This is just equal to \\( 14!^2 \\cdot \\frac{15}{2} \\). \\( \\frac{15}{2} \\) is 7.5, and 7.5 is not a perfect square, therefore option A is incorrect. \n</p><p>We can also rule that \\( \\frac{17}{2} = 8.5 \\) and \\( \\frac{19}{2} = 9.5 \\) are both not perfect squares, so option choices C and E are also incorrect. \n</p><p>If we take B. \\( \\frac{15! \\cdot 16!}{2} \\), we see that \\( 15!^2 \\) is a perfect square, but \\( \\frac{16}{2} = 8 \\) is not, so B is incorrect. Our remaining option is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69aa9273fab09663f313366e7a0cbad049d5529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{17!18!}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"97\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>Proof:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e1ca23aaa3e7528b1f60c0104d21f8becc2c15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{17! \\cdot 18!}{2} \\Rightarrow 17!^2 \\cdot \\frac{18}{2} \\Rightarrow 17!^2 \\cdot 9 \\Rightarrow 17!^2 \\cdot 3^2.\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>The product of two squares is always a perfect square.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, note that\n</p><p>\\[\n\\frac{14!\\cdot 15!}{2} = 2\\cdot 15 \\cdot (\\text{a large perfect square}).\n\\]\n</p><p>In general, for \\(\\frac{a!\\cdot b!}{2}\\) to be a perfect square, \\(2b\\) must itself be a perfect square.\n</p><p>Thus we test \\(a,b,c,d,e\\). Since \\(18 \\times 2 = 36\\) is a perfect square, the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}\\).\n</p><p>croc-012\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sa9OON6KXb8\">https://youtu.be/sa9OON6KXb8</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uY_Xp8GtXP8\">https://youtu.be/uY_Xp8GtXP8</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b>